  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "xmlTextReaderRemoveID",
    "file": "libxml2/xmlreader.c",
    "description": "Double-free is caused by ownership confusion introduced in xmlTextReaderRemoveID. When freeing an attribute, xmlTextReaderFreeProp calls xmlTextReaderRemoveID, which sets id->name = attr->name and id->attr = NULL without duplicating/interning the string. The attribute name is then freed in xmlTextReaderFreeProp (DICT_FREE(cur->name)). Later, xmlTextReaderFreeDoc frees the ID table and xmlFreeID frees id->name again, producing a double-free.",
    "conditions": "Triggered in xml reader streaming mode when a parsed attribute is recognized as an ID (here xml:id on <a xml:id=\"\"> with DTD present in input), and incremental cleanup frees nodes before document teardown. Data flow: fuzzer input -> xmlTextReaderRead parses start tag/attribute -> ID entry created -> xmlTextReaderRead cleanup path calls xmlTextReaderFreeNode/xmlTextReaderFreeProp -> xmlTextReaderRemoveID aliases id->name to attr->name -> attr->name freed -> xmlFreeTextReader/xmlTextReaderFreeDoc later frees ID table entry -> second free of same pointer."
  },
